1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,752
This knight sacrifice drags the king into the center.

2
00:00:04,912 --> 00:00:09,365
The Fried Liver starts with two natural developing moves.

3
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:13,977
White attacks the knight and forces the central break.

4
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:18,590
Black answers with a pawn hit, but the king is still uncastled.

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:23,203
The knight takes on d five and the trap is already visible.

6
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:27,815
White gives up the knight to remove the king's shelter.

7
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:32,428
The king takes, but that capture walks into a queen check.

8
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:37,040
Queen f three checks along the open file.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,652
The king has to step forward instead of castling.

10
00:00:41,812 --> 00:00:46,265
Now every developing move comes with tempo.

11
00:00:46,425 --> 00:00:50,877
The lesson: count king safety before counting material.

12
00:00:51,037 --> 00:00:55,650
Would you take the knight or decline the trap?

